  @ [support] C:\Project\Cantor\feature_support\reviews\HonestySecurityIdentityBoundaryIntegrityIntakeReview.sop
  + [core_result] boundary integrity is a shared higher-order monitor: Honesty guards semantic and epistemic identity while Security guards operational and effect identity
  + [non_reduction] Honesty retains truth correspondence and evidence obligations; Security retains harm, stability, and admissibility obligations beyond identity continuity
  + [identity_frame] is subject, meaning, epistemic status, attribution, purpose, domain, authority, scope, constraints, effect envelope, and constitutive invariants
  + [violation_shape] is concealed crossing, displacement, erosion, substitution, illicit transfer, domain capture, purpose displacement, scope expansion, constraint weakening, or effect amplification
  + [relationship_result] is association becomes warranted only through typed direction, evidence, conditions, transfer law, non-transfer set, and invalidation
  + [deception_boundary] deceptive structure may be detected without claiming human motive absent separate evidence
  + [implementation_result] is none; current static IdentityBoundary remains useful but insufficient for transition integration
  + [schedule_effect] CIFP-SLICE-02 is blocked pending HSIBI-SJS-01
  + [next] multi-authority SJS input audit before canonical schema or code

& [HonestySecurityIdentityViolationPrimitiveRevisionMilestone] strengthens the faculty common law
  @ [source] C:\Project\Cantor\source_documents\2026-08-03_hsibi_identity_violation_primitive_revision\Dictated_HSIBI_Identity_Violation_Primitive_Revision_Source.sop
